shooter's studio people can fly  announced its new game out writers at e3  last year  it's a third-person shooter that gives  you a host of cool superpowers set in a  dense and fairly dark sci-fi world we  played the first few hours of outriders  at a recent preview event in Los Angeles  and learned a heck of a lot about it  here's everything we know about  outriders so far our writers is an RPG  infused cover shooter that feels like  it's borrowing from two other people can  fly games Gears of War judgment and  bullets tour you carry three weapons  which includes two switchable primary  guns and a pair of sidearms you can use  when ammo is low the guns we saw  included assault rifles shotguns and  snipers and it seems those weapons will  carry different perks and capabilities  in my few hours with the game though  shotguns felt the best as they blow off  enemy limbs and heads in a way that  carries all the satisfaction of similar  guns in Gears of War  you can also expect to modify your  weapons and armor over time to change  how they work and their effects you'll  do a lot of shooting in outriders but  the game is main appeal is the special  powers you'll get as one of the altered  after the game's prologue when your  powers unlock you'll choose from one of  three classes the Devastator a tank like  character who can affect gravity for  seismic attacks the Pyromancer a more  mid-range fighter who can take out  multiple enemies with flame based  attacks and the trickster who bends time  and space to teleport behind enemies  slow them down and take them apart with  hit-and-run tactics it's possible to  customize your three classes throughout  the course of the game as you level up  your character thanks to an extensive  skill tree as you play you'll unlock  eight different abilities for your class  allowing you to switch between them as  you play I saw 3 during the course of  the demo and each cools down pretty  quickly so while the base of outriders  is a cover shooter your abilities allow  you to run and gun quite a bit you're  not gonna spend the whole game stuck  behind chest-high walls the thing about  the classes in outriders is that each  has a special healing mechanic which  encourages you to play to their  strengths I played as the trickster who  is healed by taking out enemies at close  range my abilities included teleporting  and with a shotgun in hand it meant I  was able to pop across the battlefield  and devastate someone while they were  still in cover heal myself up and then  take their position to flank out the  remaining enemies you can play outriders  alone but the game supports drop-in  dropout co-op for up to 3 players there  are also no limitations on classes you  can run a group of 3 tricksters if you  want or each pick a separate class and  support each other with your different  abilities you choose your class early at  the end of outriders prologue and once  you make that choice you're locked in  for the duration of the game outriders  is mostly a shooter but it also mixes in  a lot of RPG elements in the vein of  something like Mass Effect as you play  you'll constantly be coming across armor  and weapons for different stat boosts  the loot you'll find will vary in rarity  like in a lot of RPG type games these  days with better guns and armor being  tougher to come by as you level up your  character you'll also level up the  game's a world level which is  effectively a difficulty level you earn  and can set as you choose the higher  your world level the tougher the enemies  you'll encounter but the better the loot  you'll earn  the way you have to gain experience to  unlock new harder world levels but if  you're ever facing a challenge you can't  handle it you can always turn it back  down to a point you've already unlocked  my time without writers included a  prologue that set up the story and gave  a deep look at the lore of the world you  play one of the titular outriders a  character you create at the start of the  game and a member of a colony group  that's trying to spread humanity to a  new world called Enoch things were bad  back on earth with society collapsing as  resources became scarce during the  conflicts that sprung up because of  those problems outriders were a heroic  group of scientists and military types  who fought to help humanity survive on  the colony ship your job is to go down  to Enoch in the first wave of colonists  in order to secure it for everybody else  the trip to Enoch has taken 80 years and  from all accounts the rest of humanity  might have wiped itself out in that  period after landing the outriders  encounter a strange energy storm that  comes to be called the anomaly it's  completely unpredictable sometimes  annihilating anything in its path and  sometimes giving animals and humans  ridiculous powers in the prologue most  of the remaining out writers are killed  by the anomaly which also renders most  of the colonists advanced human  technology worthless after you are  zapped by the anomaly your surviving  friends throw you back into cryostasis  to save your life when you wake up again  Enoch isn't the mostly idyllic place he  left but instead has been transformed  into a war-torn hellscape turns out you  slept for 30 years and in that time the  remaining colonists were dropped onto  Enoch  only to find the anomaly killing people  and knocking out the technology  essential to survival factions have been  fighting over food and scraps ever since  with some people becoming altered making  them more or less godlike but often  corrupted by their power story seems to  be a pretty big focus for outriders with  a lot of time in the prologue spent on  dialogue between characters  okay I had that under control although  you shouldn't expect branching  storylines or conversation choices  however you will find optional side  missions to complete that will add more  depth to the main campaign which sounds  like it should clock in at about 25  hours we know one last thing about  outriders its release window expected in  holiday 2020 for ps4 Xbox one and PC as  well as PlayStation 5 and Xbox series X  so that's everything we know so far  about outriders are you excited to check  out Enoch and people can flies latest  are you looking to play the trickster  Pyromancer or Devastator leave us your  thoughts in the comments below
 

